From: Yusuf <yusufyav.dev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: keep the full EDID on hotplug

dw_hdmi_qp_cec_set_hpd() read the EDID with drm_get_edid() for the CEC
physical address only. drm_get_edid() also stores its copy as the
connector's EDID property, through drm_connector_update_edid_property(),
which sizes the blob by the base block's extension count and so drops
every block an HF-EEODB declares beyond it. get_modes() then reuses that
property instead of reading again.

A BenQ RD280UG declares three blocks through HF-EEODB, the third a
DisplayID block holding 3840x2560 at 60, 100 and 120 Hz. After the first
hotplug its EDID was 256 bytes, those modes were gone and the preferred
mode fell back to the base block's 3840x2560 at 49.98 Hz.

Read with drm_edid_read_ddc(), which leaves the property alone.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index 20d6a9393..77f001a8e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -3836,15 +3836,25 @@ void dw_hdmi_qp_cec_set_hpd(struct dw_hdmi_qp *hdmi, bool plug_in, bool change)
 	if (!plug_in)
 		cec_notifier_set_phys_addr(hdmi->cec_notifier,
 					   CEC_PHYS_ADDR_INVALID);
-       else if (hdmi->ddc) {
-               struct edid *edid = drm_get_edid(&hdmi->connector, hdmi->ddc);
-               if (edid) {
-                       if (hdmi->cec_notifier)
-                               cec_notifier_set_phys_addr_from_edid(
-                                       hdmi->cec_notifier, edid);
-                       kfree(edid);
-               }
-       }
+	else if (hdmi->ddc) {
+		/*
+		 * Read for the physical address only. drm_get_edid() would also
+		 * store this copy as the connector's EDID property, sized by the
+		 * base block's extension count: an EDID that declares further
+		 * blocks through HF-EEODB loses them, and get_modes() then
+		 * reuses the truncated property instead of reading again -- a
+		 * BenQ RD280UG lost its DisplayID block, and with it 3840x2560
+		 * at 60, 100 and 120 Hz, on every hotplug.
+		 */
+		const struct drm_edid *drm_edid =
+			drm_edid_read_ddc(&hdmi->connector, hdmi->ddc);
+
+		if (drm_edid) {
+			cec_notifier_set_phys_addr_from_edid(hdmi->cec_notifier,
+							     drm_edid_raw(drm_edid));
+			drm_edid_free(drm_edid);
+		}
+	}
 
 	if (hdmi->bridge.dev) {
 #if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_DRM_DW_HDMI_CEC)
